Serve /tokenize and /detokenize under /v1 as well as at the root.

Every OpenAI SDK client (and most gateways) points base_url at a URL ending
in /v1 and resolves every endpoint relative to it, so the root-only routes
were a genuine 404 for them: the tokenization endpoints were unusable from
stock clients. The router is now included twice, once as-is and once with
prefix="/v1"; FastAPI derives each route's operation id from name + path +
method, so the two mounts carry distinct ids (tokenize_tokenize_post /
tokenize_v1_tokenize_post) and the OpenAPI schema stays valid.

